                        "text":  {
                                     "text":  "Another neighbourhood gem, well off the usual tourist trail. The sushi, sashimi, donburi, and grilled and fried dishes are all of impressively high quality, especially given the reasonable prices. Beer options are fairly limited—only one Taiwanese beer and Kirin—but that hardly detracts from the experience. As with many Taipei neighbourhood spots, seating is on the cramped side, and it can get quite busy during peak dining hours.",
